course: dictionary
lesson: 8588
title: One word, two meanings: scoff
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. «Who scoffed all the biscuits?» Here scoff means eat very quickly and greedily, because the biscuits have all gone.
explain: Scoff can also mean to laugh at something in a mocking way, as if it were silly. In a story, people might scoff at an inventor's idea, so they laugh at it and say it will never work. Ask yourself: is the sentence about someone eating, or someone laughing and mocking?
explain: Check by trying your meaning in the sentence. "Who laughed all the biscuits?" makes no sense, so eating is right there. When a word has more than one meaning, the context decides.
fact: Scoff is a verb with the forms scoffs, scoffed and scoffing.
fact: To scoff at someone or something means to laugh at it in a mocking way, as if it were silly.
fact: In British and Australian informal speech, to scoff food means to eat it very quickly and greedily.
fact: In UK slang, scoff can also be a noun meaning food.
fact: Useful phrases: scoff at, scoff down, scoff the lot.
exercise: «Who scoffed all the biscuits?» What does scoffed mean here? | Packed them away neatly | *Ate them very quickly | Counted them carefully | Laughed at them
exercise: The crowd began to scoff at the inventor's strange machine. What does scoff at mean? | Fixed it carefully | Cheered it loudly | *Laughed at it in a mocking way | Bought it for a friend
exercise: Sam said, «I'm going to scoff the lot before the bus comes.» What does scoff the lot suggest? | Throw everything away | *Eat everything quickly and greedily | Share everything kindly with friends | Save everything for later
test: Why did the coach scoff at the team's plan? | *Because he thought it was silly and mocked it | Because he wrote it down | Because he wanted to eat it | Because he cheered it on
test: Which sentence uses scoff to mean eat greedily? | The crowd began to scoff at the clown's tricks. | Nobody would scoff at a brilliant idea. | Dad said the plan would never work and began to scoff. | *Ella scoffed her sandwich in two bites before the bell.
exam: What does scoff mean in «Stop scoffing those crisps, they're mine!»? | Laughing at the crisps | *Eating the crisps quickly and greedily | Counting the crisps | Throwing the crisps away
